        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.11.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.11.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Reu lived after he begat Serug two hundred and seven years, and begat sons and daughters.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.11.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.11.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Serug lived thirty years, and begat Nahor:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.11.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.11.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Serug lived after he begat Nahor two hundred years, and begat sons and daughters.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.11.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.11.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Nahor lived nine and twenty years, and begat Terah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.11.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.11.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Nahor lived after he begat Terah a hundred and nineteen years, and begat sons and daughters.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.11.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.11.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Terah lived seventy years, and begat Abram, Nahor, and Haran.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.11.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.11.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the generations of Terah: Terah begat Abram, Nahor, and Haran: and Haran begat Lot.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.11.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.11.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Haran died before his father Terah, in the land of his nativity, in Ur of the Chaldees.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.11.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.11.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Abram and Nahor took them wives: the name of Abram's wife ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Sarai; and the name of Nahor's wife Milcah, the daughter of Haran, the father of Milcah, and the father of Iscah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.11.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.11.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Sarai ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " barren; she had no child.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.11.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.11.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Terah took Abram his son, and Lot the son of Haran his son's son, and Sarai his daughter-in-law, his son Abram's wife; and they went forth with them from Ur of the Chaldees, to go into the land of Canaan; and they came to Haran, and dwelt there.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.11.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.11.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the days of Terah were two hundred and five years: and Terah died in Haran.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
